{"step_index":220,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-11T15:04:59Z","thinking":"**Applying `minCard_le` to problem**\n\nThe `minCard_le` result can directly prove an upper bound on the `totalDominationNumber`. It leverages the property `GraphCalc.IsTotalDominatingSet` to establish that the minimum cardinality of a total dominating set is less than or equal to the cardinality of any such set. Therefore, this yields the desired theorem about the total domination number.\n\n\n**Reducing Roman domination problem**\n\nThe problem reduces to showing that for any Roman dominating function `f`, a total dominating set exists with cardinality less than or equal to the Roman weight of `f`. This conclusion relies on showing the image of Roman weights is non-empty, which holds since a constant function always exists. Establishing this relationship would then complete the reduction.\n\n\n**Constructing Total Dominating Set**\n\nThe goal is constructing a total dominating set `s` with bounded cardinality.  The existence of a total dominating set is guaranteed by `h_has`. This means `∃ s ∈ univ.powerset, GraphCalc.IsTotalDominatingSet G s`. `exists_adj_of_has_td` confirms every vertex has a neighbor.\n\nThis leads to the definition of a neighbor function `nbr` chosen using `Classical.choose`.  `nbr` maps each vertex to one of its neighbors, establishing `G.Adj v (nbr v)`. The symmetry of adjacency yields `G.Adj (nbr v) v` as well.\n\nNow defining sets `V_2` (where f(v) = 2) and `V_1` (where f(v)=1) is next.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"\"cat << 'EOF' >> scratch.lean\\n\\ntheorem romanWeight_eq {V : Type} [Fintype V] [DecidableEq V] (f : V → Fin 3) :\\n    GraphCalc.romanWeight f = 2 * (Finset.univ.filter (fun v => f v = 2)).card +\\n      (Finset.univ.filter (fun v => f v = 1)).card := by\\n  unfold GraphCalc.romanWeight\\n  have h_part : Finset.univ =\\n      (Finset.univ.filter (fun v => f v = 0)) ∪\\n      (Finset.univ.filter (fun v => f v = 1)) ∪\\n      (Finset.univ.filter (fun v => f v = 2)) := by\\n    ext v\\n    simp only [Finset.mem_univ, Finset.mem_union, Finset.mem_filter, true_and]\\n    have : f v = 0 ∨ f v = 1 ∨ f v = 2 := by\\n      fin_cases f v <;> simp\\n    tauto\\n  sorry\\nEOF\\n/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/tools/antigravity/check.sh scratch.lean\"","Cwd":"\"/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/handoff/promising13/task_40a99333\"","WaitMsBeforeAsync":"10000","toolAction":"\"Testing fin_cases on Fin 3 in scratch.lean\"","toolSummary":"\"Check fin_cases on Fin 3\""}}]}
